      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Storing high volumes of flammable solvents in high-density racking presents significant risks. Poor ventilation can lead to the accumulation of flammable vapors, reaching explosive concentrations within the warehouse air. Furthermore, if the solvents are susceptible to exothermic reactions, high density increases the potential for widespread thermal runaway if one container ignites, leading to a rapid, intense fire. Proper segregation, fire suppression systems, and continuous monitoring of ambient and localized temperatures are crucial mitigating factors.",
