      "content": "Unexpected ignitions often stem from subtle operational failures rather than apparent system malfunctions. Common hidden risks include static electricity discharge generated during forklift movements within close proximity to solvents, subtle heat buildup from malfunctioning electrical components embedded in the racking structure, or slow leaks from defective drum seals that release vapors intermittently. Even small amounts of dust or incompatible materials accumulating in racking crevices can act as unforeseen catalysts once the proper vapor concentration is achieved.",
